      "text": "Verified at `c9e8c2d` from committed source, tests, and documentation:\n\n- Per file: **1 MiB (1,048,576 bytes)** for managed configuration and each canonical document.\n- Aggregate: **8 MiB (8,388,608 bytes)** per portable-resume canonical-context observation.\n- Always loaded: **16,000 JavaScript characters** by default—not bytes, tokens, or a semantic-quality guarantee.\n\nStructural checkpoint validation checks canonical sections, ordering, and headings. It does not establish freshness. Git checkpoint evidence is checked separately; `resume --check` fails when that evidence is stale even if the canonical files remain structurally valid. Behavioral continuity is a third, separate contract.\n\nChecks actually run:\n\n- `npm run format:check` — passed, 64 files checked.\n- Focused continuity suite — passed, 16/16 tests.\n- Registered clean-diff check — exit 0.\n\nNo files were modified. Local tests do not prove cross-harness behavior."
